# Local development & database

The maintainer runs the stack locally against the **production Turso database** on purpose (`backend/.dev.vars` with prod credentials). Do not insist on a separate dev database unless they ask.

## When helping with local dev

- Assume `npm run dev:local` (frontend + API) or `.env.local` with `VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787` is the normal workflow.
- Production API default (`https://api.eypi.cc`) applies only when `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is unset at build time — do not change that default.

## Safety (still required)

Even with production DB access, **do not** add or run destructive changes unless the user explicitly requests them:

- No `DELETE`, `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, or bulk updates without clear user approval
- No migration scripts that wipe or reset tables unless asked
- No committing secrets (`.env.local`, `backend/.dev.vars`)

Schema additions and non-destructive reads/writes for feature work are fine.

## Secrets

Never commit or log `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN`, `JWT_SECRET`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, or wallet keys. Example templates (`.env.example`, `.dev.vars.example`) only.
